session:pr739Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #723 identified that build_openapi() in sparql_endpoint/src/openapi.rs had fallen behind the routes actually wired in server.rs, and that docs/plans/OPENAPI_FRONTEND_386_PLAN.md's route-coverage list had drifted further and claimed some of those gaps were already covered. Confirmed the gap by reading server.rs's build_router() route-by-route against openapi.rs's PathsBuilder calls: GET/POST /$/ready, GET/HEAD /{name}/get, GET /.well-known/void, POST /upload, GET /describe, GET /id/{path}, GET /ns/agentprov/session, and GET /vqs/productive-values were all wired but undocumented, and HEAD was missing from the GSP-shaped routes (/rdf-graph-store, /rdf-graphs/{path}, /{name}/data) even though server.rs wires .head(...) handlers for all three. Added PathItems for each missing route and a head operation inside gsp_path_item/dataset_data_path_item, following the existing hand-built utoipa::openapi::OpenApiBuilder pattern rather than introducing a new one (op()/item1()/merge() helpers, query_param()/path_param() for parameters, the existing ok_rdf_response/ok_plain_json_response/no_content_response helpers for bodies) so the new entries read the same as the ones #386/#517 already added. /$/ready got its own admin_ready_path_item() rather than reusing simple_get, since (like /$/ping) it is wired with both GET and POST against the same admin_ping handler and simple_get only builds a GET operation. Corrected OPENAPI_FRONTEND_386_PLAN.md's 'Route coverage' list to stop claiming /$/ready and /.well-known/void were covered by the first pass, and added a '## Follow-up coverage (#723)' section mirroring the existing #517 one. Extended sparql_endpoint/tests/openapi_docs.rs with openapi_json_lists_723_routes, an HTTP-level test (hitting GET /api-docs/openapi.json, matching the file's existing test style) asserting each new path+method is present, plus HEAD on the three GSP-shaped paths, so a future route wired in server.rs but missing from build_openapi() is caught by CI rather than relying on another manual side-by-side read." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:739 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr739 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
